2.
Definitions.-
In these Rules, unless the context otherwise requires,-
(a)
"Act" means the Cost and Works Accountants Act, 1959;
(b)
"aggrieved person" means a person who contested that election to the Council to which the dispute pertains;
(c)
"dispute" means a dispute raised by an aggrieved person arising out of the election to the Council of the Institute;
(d)
"election" means election to the Council held under sub-section (2) of section 9 of the Act;
(e)
"legal practitioner" means a person registered with Bar Council of India or any of the State Bar Councils and is eligible to
appear before a Court of law;
(f)
"Tribunal" means the Tribunal formed under sub-section (1) of section 10-B of the Act.
